# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets and local state out
# of it: anything listed here can never be copied into an image by accident.
.git
.github
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local state and build artifacts — rebuilt inside the image, and copying them in would
# shadow the container's own paths (a host venv is the wrong interpreter entirely).
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info
apps/api/var
apps/api/test_meyraki.db
**/.pytest_cache
# The test suite has no business in a production image, and it carries qa_hunt.py and
# golden_set.py — both of which spend model credits if anyone runs them in there.
apps/api/tests
scripts
apps/web/test-results
apps/web/playwright-report

# Founder deliverables and scratch output — large, regenerated, never part of a build.
artifacts
docs
*.md
!README.md
